cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Version 0.1.0 of this research repository."
title: "A skew Hadamard matrix of order 2120"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/skew-hadamard-2120"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/skew-hadamard-2120"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A paper and release repository giving a skew Hadamard matrix of order
  2120 = 2^3 * 265. No earlier published construction at this order was
  found in the sources checked; Cati and Pasechnik record 4240 as the least
  known skew order with odd part 265, and the 2025 census of Dokovic and
  Seberry lists order 1060 as undecided. The matrix comes from four sign
  patterns on the field with 529 elements, fixed by eight signs on the
  projective line over F_23, whose Fourier energies sum to a constant; eight
  integer character sums certify the construction, and a bordered
  Goethals-Seidel array gives the matrix. A vector form of Turyn's cyclic
  expansion carries such seeds to every odd power, giving skew Hadamard
  matrices of order 4(p^(2n)+1) for p = 7, 23, 263 and every odd n. Four is
  the least number of blocks for an all-skew family on these groups. The
  archived matrix is checked exactly. Novelty is bounded to the sources
  searched.
keywords:
  - Hadamard matrices
  - skew Hadamard matrices
  - supplementary difference sets
  - Gauss sums
  - Goethals-Seidel array
  - Turyn cyclic expansion
